SUMMARY:Women in ECE: AI and the Future of Work
DESCRIPTION:November 3 @ 12:00 pm – 2:00 pm \n\nJoin us for Women in ECE: AI and the Future of Work\, an engaging conversation exploring how artificial intelligence is reshaping engineering\, careers and the workplace. \nHosted by Professor Deepa Kundur\, Chair of ECE\, the event will bring together students\, alumni and industry leaders to discuss how AI is changing the way we work\, the skills engineers will need in the years ahead and how students can prepare for an increasingly AI-enabled future. \nThrough an interactive panel discussion\, speakers will share their perspectives on evolving career pathways\, the role of human expertise and the opportunities and challenges AI presents for the next generation of engineers. \nRegistration Deadline: Friday\, October 30\, 2026
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/women-in-ece-ai-and-the-future-of-work/
LOCATION:Galbraith Building\, Room 202 (GB202)\, 35 St George\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1A4\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
