SUMMARY:RJC Career Information Session – Interested in structural engineering and building science?
DESCRIPTION:Interested in structural engineering and building science?\nWednesday\, November 4\, 2026  5-7 p.m.\nin BA2155\, Bahen Centre\nRegister: RJC Career Information Session\nPIZZA PROVIDED \nJoin us on for an industry talk with RJC\, one of North America’s premier engineering firms. Since 1948\, RJC has expanded from a small structural engineering practice into a multidisciplinary organization delivering innovative solutions across Canada and the United States. \nCome to hear from Duncan Rowe and James Cooper\, both U of T alumni and industry professionals\, to learn about exciting projects\, and explore potential career opportunities. \nBios\nDuncan Rowe (CivE 0T4\, MEng 0T9) is a Principal at Read Jones Christoffersen with over 20 years of experience in building envelope design\, assessment\, and rehabilitation. He holds a Bachelor of Applied Science and a Certificate in Preventative Engineering from the University of Toronto (2004)\, and a Master’s in Building Science (2010). Since joining RJC in 2007\, Duncan has led numerous new construction projects\, with a focus on Building Enclosure Commissioning and Durability. Promoted to Project Engineer in 2010\, Associate in 2015\, and Principal in 2020\, Duncan brings deep technical expertise in various building envelope systems. He also serves on the national code commission for Part 5 of the National Building Code. \nJames Cooper (CivE 0T5) is a Principal at Read Jones Christoffersen and a Licensed Professional Engineer in Ontario. He graduated with honours from the University of Toronto in 2005 and joined RJC the same year. He became a Project Engineer in 2010\, Associate in 2016\, and Principal in 2021. James has played a key role in many of RJC’s major rehabilitation and retrofit projects. He is a LEED® Accredited Professional with a specialty in Operations and Maintenance of existing buildings and is currently pursuing certification as a Construction Contract Administrator. He manages projects through all phases—from pre-design to close-out—with a focus on sustainable and effective building performance.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/rjc-career-information-session-interested-in-structural-engineering-and-building-science/
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
