SUMMARY:Hong Kong: Celebrating Daisy Ho\, 2026 Rose Wolfe Distinguished Alumni Award Recipient
DESCRIPTION:Daisy Ho (MBA 1990)\, a longtime University of Toronto volunteer\, adviser and philanthropist who has helped generations of Hong Kong students pursue a life-changing education at U of T\, is the recipient of the 2026 Rose Wolfe Distinguished Alumni Award.(opens in new tab) \nChair of the U of T (Hong Kong) Foundation\, Daisy is being recognized for her outstanding leadership\, generosity and service to the U of T community. \nPlease join David Palmer\, Vice-President\, Advancement\, and Barbara Dick\, Assistant Vice-President\, Alumni Relations\, along with the U of T community in Hong Kong\, for a special reception to celebrate Daisy Ho. \nAmong the highest honours bestowed upon alumni\, the Rose Wolfe Distinguished Alumni Award celebrates individuals whose contributions epitomize the values championed by Chancellor Emerita and fellow volunteer Dr. Rose Wolfe. \nHelp us recognize Daisy’s remarkable contributions. \n\nDoors open: 4:00 p.m.\nRemarks: 4:30 p.m.\nRefreshment will be served\nRSVP by November 2\n\nEvent hosted by the University of Toronto and the U of T Alumni Association. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHave questions about this event? Contact Prudence Ng at ask@utoronto.com.hk
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/hong-kong-celebrating-daisy-ho-2026-rose-wolfe-distinguished-alumni-award-recipient/
LOCATION:Four Seasons Hotel Hong Kong
CATEGORIES:Alumni events
END:VEVENT
